## 🎨 Title  
ML5 Pong with Handpose 

---

## ✨ Description  
Explain the inspiration for your sketch.  
Why did you choose this idea?
I wanted to use ML5's hand tracking as soon as I saw the example shown in class. 
I knew I wanted to do something different from what the example was so I chose something 
relatively simple, pong. The pong game itself was easy to create so I was able to spend my 
time integrating the handpose. 

---

## ⚙️ Setup  
How should someone run your code?  
My code should be ran in a browser. When asked for permission to access the camera, choose "Allow." 
Having volume on is recommended as well. 

What technologies, libraries, or tools did you use (e.g., p5.js, ml5.js, audio features, AI tools)?  
I used VS Code to create my project. The libraries I used were p5.js and ML5.js. The webpage was built
in HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

---

## 🔍 Reflection  
How could you improve or extend your project in the future?  
In the future I would have liked to be able to create a wireframe of the hand's structure so that my program 
could be used without the camera if the user would rather not have it on. 

What challenges did you face while building it?  
The biggest challenge I faced while building my project was deciding what to create. I had many ideas and created
a few prototypes before I settled on this one.

Do you have any critiques, suggestions, or opinions about p5.js or this assignment?  
I enjoyed using p5.js. I found it intuitive and had what I needed to create my project. I think the project was also
very interesting because it was a perfect mix of graphics and computer science. 

